From 8c44d632fc0d11cf3dc39b49befe405d750b3d64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 07:19:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] WIP audit/vod: the film's buffer is sized again once room
 has been made (pages' pictures, the last episode's buffer)

The player is built about half a second after OK, before the page it started from has let go of its pictures and
before Android has collected the buffer of the film or episode before, so the free-memory rule held the buffer down
for memory that was on its way back. FilmRoom collects at once when something big is let go of and tells the film's
player, which reads the free memory again (only ever more, up to the tier's size).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
